      "message": "net: parse NAT-PMP result code as 16-bit BE in PCP fallback\n\nWhen checking whether a gateway replied with NAT-PMP unsupported version (RFC 6887 appendix A and RFC 6886 section 3.5), PCPRequestPortMap mistakenly used PCP_RESPONSE_HDR_RESULT_OFS (3) and compared only a single byte against NATPMP_RESULT_UNSUPP_VERSION.\n\nNAT-PMP result codes are 16-bit big-endian values starting at offset 2 (NATPMP_RESPONSE_HDR_RESULT_OFS). A 16-bit result code with low byte 1 and a non-zero high byte (such as 0x0101) would previously be incorrectly treated as UNSUPP_VERSION.\n\nUse ReadBE16 with NATPMP_RESPONSE_HDR_RESULT_OFS instead, matching the rest of pcp.cpp, and use NATPMP_HDR_VERSION_OFS for the version check. Add a unit test covering this case.",
